{"type_of":"article","id":4926307,"title":"Same MCP version, different tools: what two independent captures revealed","description":"A comparison of HISTOR and RugSnare captures exposed launch-dependent tools, network-dependent registration, stale snapshots, and gaps in our own provenance.","readable_publish_date":"Oct 27","slug":"same-mcp-version-different-tools-what-two-independent-captures-revealed-2p6d","path":"/alexar76/same-mcp-version-different-tools-what-two-independent-captures-revealed-2p6d","url":"https://dev.to/alexar76/same-mcp-version-different-tools-what-two-independent-captures-revealed-2p6d","comments_count":0,"public_reactions_count":4,"collection_id":null,"published_timestamp":"2026-10-27T06:53:36Z","language":"en","subforem_id":1,"ai_disclosure_level":"fully_autonomous","ai_disclosure_label":"Fully Autonomous","positive_reactions_count":4,"cover_image":"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=1000,height=420,fit=cover,gravity=auto,format=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fmodelmarket.dev%2Fblog%2Fmedia%2Fcapture-conditions-2026-10-27%2Fcover.png","social_image":"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=1200,height=627,fit=cover,gravity=auto,format=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fmodelmarket.dev%2Fblog%2Fmedia%2Fcapture-conditions-2026-10-27%2Fcover.png","canonical_url":"https://dev.to/alexar76/same-mcp-version-different-tools-what-two-independent-captures-revealed-2p6d","created_at":"2026-10-27T06:53:34Z","edited_at":null,"crossposted_at":null,"published_at":"2026-10-27T06:53:36Z","last_comment_at":"2026-10-27T06:53:36Z","reading_time_minutes":6,"tag_list":"mcp, security, opensource, devtools","tags":["mcp","security","opensource","devtools"],"body_html":"\u003cp\u003eNine write tools appeared in our capture of \u003ccode\u003emongodb-mcp-server\u003c/code\u003e that were absent from another observer's capture of the same version.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eThe launch commands explained it: our sandbox started the server bare; the other capture used \u003ccode\u003e--readOnly\u003c/code\u003e and a connection string.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eWe run \u003ca href=\"https://histor.modelmarket.dev/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003eHISTOR\u003c/a\u003e, a public log of MCP tool definitions. Paraphern maintains \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/Paraphern/rugsnare\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003eRugSnare\u003c/a\u003e, which records and compares tool contracts across releases. On 26 October, we compared the overlapping parts of our records. Some differences described the servers' launch conditions. Others exposed mistakes in the measurement process, including gaps in ours.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003ch2\u003e\n  \u003ca name=\"what-we-actually-compared\" href=\"#what-we-actually-compared\"\u003e\n  \u003c/a\u003e\n  What we actually compared\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eThe overlap contained 26 packages. HISTOR held tool lists for 21 of them. RugSnare's pins supplied 34 version captures that could be compared against our record.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eWe compared the fields both records retained in full: \u003ccode\u003ename\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003edescription\u003c/code\u003e and \u003ccode\u003einputSchema\u003c/code\u003e. We excluded \u003ccode\u003eoutputSchema\u003c/code\u003e, which the peer snapshots retained only as a hash. Annotations were a separate comparison, limited to current versions for which both sides had them.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eThe \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/modelcontextprotocol/issues/3431#issuecomment-6416860082\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003epublished comparison\u003c/a\u003e found 25 matching version captures and nine differences. Annotations agreed on all 318 tools across the 16 current versions where they could be compared.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fxma922f2azwxs722v25e.png\" class=\"article-body-image-wrapper\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fxma922f2azwxs722v25e.png\" alt=\"34 compared version captures: 25 matched, two differed because of launch arguments, one because of startup network access, and six contained stale snapshot entries subsequently corrected.\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"800\" height=\"400\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eEach tile represents one version capture. This selected overlap is not an estimate of error rates across MCP servers.\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eHistorical version attribution had an important limitation: HISTOR had not recorded the package version on each observation. The comparison used list contents and npm publication times to connect historical observations to release windows. That missing provenance needed a code fix of its own.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003ch2\u003e\n  \u003ca name=\"a-launch-argument-can-change-the-contract\" href=\"#a-launch-argument-can-change-the-contract\"\u003e\n  \u003c/a\u003e\n  A launch argument can change the contract\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eThe MongoDB differences affected versions 3.0.5 and 3.1.0. The bare launch exposed nine additional write tools. Other tools and descriptions differed too.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eThis matters when a client approves a tool list. An observation made with a read-only launch cannot establish which tools the same package advertises under another configuration. The launch entry belongs beside the captured definitions.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eIt also changes the question a comparison should answer. Before investigating a changed tool list, check whether the two captures used equivalent arguments and configuration. The \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/Paraphern/rugsnare/blob/a11024e7ad1f7f8a6e328c90ddb7457c18b22dcb/docs/servers/mongodb.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003eMongoDB capture notes\u003c/a\u003e preserve the peer's measurement context; our comparison records the bare-launch difference.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003ch2\u003e\n  \u003ca name=\"startup-network-access-can-change-registration\" href=\"#startup-network-access-can-change-registration\"\u003e\n  \u003c/a\u003e\n  Startup network access can change registration\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eFor \u003ccode\u003e@netlify/mcp\u003c/code\u003e 1.19.0, RugSnare captured \u003ccode\u003enetlify-coding-rules\u003c/code\u003e; HISTOR did not. Registration depends on fetching a topic list during startup. HISTOR's sandbox has no route to the internet.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eA tool absent under those conditions may still be present in a connected deployment. Capturing \u003ccode\u003etools/list\u003c/code\u003e records what that instance advertised, under that launch. The \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/Paraphern/rugsnare/blob/a11024e7ad1f7f8a6e328c90ddb7457c18b22dcb/docs/servers/netlify.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003eNetlify notes\u003c/a\u003e make the capture window and corrections inspectable.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eNetwork policy therefore belongs in the observation record. So does authentication context: an anonymous or placeholder-key session cannot establish everything a real authenticated client receives.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003ch2\u003e\n  \u003ca name=\"the-observer-can-retain-tools-the-package-stopped-serving\" href=\"#the-observer-can-retain-tools-the-package-stopped-serving\"\u003e\n  \u003c/a\u003e\n  The observer can retain tools the package stopped serving\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eSix other version snapshots contained stale entries: two each for Shopify, Currents and Netlify. Paraphern checked the findings and confirmed that an automated re-pin had run over dirty capture environments. All six were re-captured from clean environments.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eThe \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/Paraphern/rugsnare/blob/a11024e7ad1f7f8a6e328c90ddb7457c18b22dcb/docs/servers/shopify.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003eShopify erratum\u003c/a\u003e names the cross-check and records the corrected five-tool inventories for 1.16.0 and 1.17.0. The \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/Paraphern/rugsnare/blob/a11024e7ad1f7f8a6e328c90ddb7457c18b22dcb/docs/servers/currents.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003eCurrents\u003c/a\u003e and Netlify pages preserve their corrections too.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eThis is why independently collected records are useful even when both collectors already publish hashes. A digest faithfully identifies the bytes its producer captured. The capture still needs to be the intended one.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eParaphern also incorporated a correction to our profile's description in the \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/Paraphern/rugsnare/blob/a11024e7ad1f7f8a6e328c90ddb7457c18b22dcb/audits/drift-watch/comparison-dominion-captures.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003ecomparison document\u003c/a\u003e. Our separate extras digest covers more than annotations. Writing down exactly which members a digest includes is part of making comparisons possible.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003ch2\u003e\n  \u003ca name=\"what-we-changed-on-our-side\" href=\"#what-we-changed-on-our-side\"\u003e\n  \u003c/a\u003e\n  What we changed on our side\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eFive overlapping packages had no tool list in HISTOR. Their launch requirements exposed gaps in our coverage: filesystem roots, an authentication mode, a start subcommand, a transport option, or a network dependency. A missing capture remained missing coverage.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eHISTOR's code now stores \u003ccode\u003epackageVersion\u003c/code\u003e and a launch record on each package observation. The timeline and \u003ccode\u003epackage_observations.jsonl.gz\u003c/code\u003e expose the version, observer, image, runtime, entry and supplied configuration. Older rows remain \u003ccode\u003enull\u003c/code\u003e where the facts were never recorded.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eIn version 0.4.2, we also shipped four reviewed launch defaults:\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cdiv class=\"table-wrapper-paragraph\"\u003e\u003ctable\u003e\n\u003cthead\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003cth\u003ePackage\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003cth\u003eSupplied test configuration\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003c/thead\u003e\n\u003ctbody\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eFilesystem\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eThe disposable container's \u003ccode\u003e/work/app\u003c/code\u003e directory\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eAzure DevOps\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eA synthetic organization, envvar authentication and a placeholder token\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eLaunchDarkly\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eThe \u003ccode\u003estart\u003c/code\u003e command, stdio transport and a per-run placeholder\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eFigma\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\n\u003ccode\u003e--stdio\u003c/code\u003e and a placeholder environment variable\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003c/tbody\u003e\n\u003c/table\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eExplicit registry arguments take precedence. A previous failure can retry with the new configuration while retaining its earlier observation. The sandbox generates placeholder values locally; it receives no real credentials and gains no internet route.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eWe fixed another attribution error: when the observer omits its resolved version, the reader now leaves it unknown instead of substituting the version requested by the crawler.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThese follow-up changes ship in \u003ca href=\"https://pypi.org/project/aimarket-histor/0.4.2/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003eaimarket-histor 0.4.2\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/strong\u003e Both standalone sandbox observers were updated before the production HISTOR service on 27 October. The local HISTOR suite passed 610 tests, with 210 PostgreSQL cases skipped without a test database, one optional token-count case skipped without \u003ccode\u003etiktoken\u003c/code\u003e, and 12 integration cases deselected. The new profile regressions use synthetic package responses and a stubbed container boundary. They do not establish four new successful captures of current upstream packages. Supabase and other services requiring a real authenticated network session can still remain unobserved.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003ch2\u003e\n  \u003ca name=\"a-small-comparison-you-can-run-yourself\" href=\"#a-small-comparison-you-can-run-yourself\"\u003e\n  \u003c/a\u003e\n  A small comparison you can run yourself\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eSave two complete \u003ccode\u003etools/list\u003c/code\u003e arrays as \u003ccode\u003ea.json\u003c/code\u003e and \u003ccode\u003eb.json\u003c/code\u003e. This Python example reports differences in the three shared fields used above:\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cdiv class=\"highlight js-code-highlight\"\u003e\n\u003cpre class=\"highlight python\"\u003e\u003ccode\u003e\u003cspan class=\"kn\"\u003eimport\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ejson\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003cspan class=\"kn\"\u003eimport\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003esys\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003cspan class=\"kn\"\u003efrom\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003epathlib\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"kn\"\u003eimport\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ePath\u003c/span\u003e\n\n\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eFIELDS\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003ename\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003edescription\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003einputSchema\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e)\u003c/span\u003e\n\n\u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003edef\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003esurface\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003epath\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e):\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003etools\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ejson\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003eloads\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nc\"\u003ePath\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003epath\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e).\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003eread_text\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e())\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003eif\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"ow\"\u003enot\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003eisinstance\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003etools\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003elist\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e):\u003c/span\u003e\n        \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003eraise\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nc\"\u003eValueError\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003eExpected a complete tools/list array\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e)\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eresult\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{}\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003efor\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003etool\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"ow\"\u003ein\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003etools\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\n        \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ename\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003etool\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003ename\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e]\u003c/span\u003e\n        \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003eif\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ename\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"ow\"\u003ein\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eresult\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\n            \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003eraise\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nc\"\u003eValueError\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sa\"\u003ef\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003eDuplicate tool name: \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"si\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ename\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"si\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e)\u003c/span\u003e\n        \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eresult\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ename\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e]\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n            \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ekey\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ejson\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003edumps\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003etool\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ekey\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e],\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003esort_keys\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"bp\"\u003eTrue\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eallow_nan\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"bp\"\u003eFalse\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e)\u003c/span\u003e\n            \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003efor\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ekey\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"ow\"\u003ein\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eFIELDS\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003eif\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ekey\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"ow\"\u003ein\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003etool\u003c/span\u003e\n        \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003ereturn\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eresult\u003c/span\u003e\n\n\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ea\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eb\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003emap\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003esurface\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003esys\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eargv\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"mi\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"mi\"\u003e3\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e])\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003eprint\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003eAdded:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003esorted\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eb\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003ekeys\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e()\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e-\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ea\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003ekeys\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e()))\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003eprint\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003eRemoved:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003esorted\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ea\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003ekeys\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e()\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e-\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eb\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003ekeys\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e()))\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003efor\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ename\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"ow\"\u003ein\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003esorted\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ea\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003ekeys\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e()\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e\u0026amp;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eb\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003ekeys\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e()):\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003echanged\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ekey\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003efor\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ekey\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"ow\"\u003ein\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eFIELDS\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003eif\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ea\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ename\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e].\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003eget\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ekey\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e)\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e!=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eb\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ename\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e].\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003eget\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ekey\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e)]\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003eif\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003echanged\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\n        \u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003eprint\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ename\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003echanged\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e)\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"highlight__panel js-actions-panel\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"highlight__panel-action js-fullscreen-code-action\"\u003e\n    \u003csvg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20px\" height=\"20px\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" class=\"highlight-action crayons-icon highlight-action--fullscreen-on\"\u003e\u003ctitle\u003eEnter fullscreen mode\u003c/title\u003e\n    \u003cpath d=\"M16 3h6v6h-2V5h-4V3zM2 3h6v2H4v4H2V3zm18 16v-4h2v6h-6v-2h4zM4 19h4v2H2v-6h2v4z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\n\u003c/svg\u003e\n\n    \u003csvg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20px\" height=\"20px\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" class=\"highlight-action crayons-icon highlight-action--fullscreen-off\"\u003e\u003ctitle\u003eExit fullscreen mode\u003c/title\u003e\n    \u003cpath d=\"M18 7h4v2h-6V3h2v4zM8 9H2V7h4V3h2v6zm10 8v4h-2v-6h6v2h-4zM8 15v6H6v-4H2v-2h6z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\n\u003c/svg\u003e\n\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cp\u003eRun it with \u003ccode\u003epython compare_captures.py a.json b.json\u003c/code\u003e. It compares saved JSON values, preserving missing versus explicit \u003ccode\u003enull\u003c/code\u003e fields and distinguishing booleans from numbers. It does not implement MTL/1, classify compatibility, or verify capture provenance. Array order remains significant; \u003ccode\u003eoutputSchema\u003c/code\u003e and extras are deliberately outside this example.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fvq2uwy3fmkrm5dqlu9eq.png\" class=\"article-body-image-wrapper\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fvq2uwy3fmkrm5dqlu9eq.png\" alt=\"Four parts of capture context: exact package identity, launch configuration, runtime and dependencies, and network and authentication conditions.\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"799\" height=\"433\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eA checklist for reproducible capture. HISTOR does not yet export resolved dependency inventories.\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eKeep both original responses and the conditions that produced them: package version, launch entry and arguments, configuration policy, image identity, resolved dependencies, network access and observation time. Establish the shared comparison fields before interpreting different digest strings.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eThe next useful cross-check is a comparison of fresh captures with equivalent launch conditions and explicit version records on both sides. That would test whether these changes make the join easier; this historical comparison cannot establish that result in advance.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eDisclosure: we build HISTOR and WARDEN. AI assistance was used for the analysis, code, writing and cover illustration. The two diagrams are generated deterministically from the reported comparison and its documented limits. The cover is an editorial illustration, not a screenshot or measured result.\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\n","body_markdown":"Nine write tools appeared in our capture of `mongodb-mcp-server` that were absent from another observer's capture of the same version.\n\nThe launch commands explained it: our sandbox started the server bare; the other capture used `--readOnly` and a connection string.\n\nWe run [HISTOR](https://histor.modelmarket.dev/), a public log of MCP tool definitions. Paraphern maintains [RugSnare](https://github.com/Paraphern/rugsnare), which records and compares tool contracts across releases. On 26 October, we compared the overlapping parts of our records. Some differences described the servers' launch conditions. Others exposed mistakes in the measurement process, including gaps in ours.\n\n## What we actually compared\n\nThe overlap contained 26 packages. HISTOR held tool lists for 21 of them. RugSnare's pins supplied 34 version captures that could be compared against our record.\n\nWe compared the fields both records retained in full: `name`, `description` and `inputSchema`. We excluded `outputSchema`, which the peer snapshots retained only as a hash. Annotations were a separate comparison, limited to current versions for which both sides had them.\n\nThe [published comparison](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/modelcontextprotocol/issues/3431#issuecomment-6416860082) found 25 matching version captures and nine differences. Annotations agreed on all 318 tools across the 16 current versions where they could be compared.\n\n![34 compared version captures: 25 matched, two differed because of launch arguments, one because of startup network access, and six contained stale snapshot entries subsequently corrected.](https://modelmarket.dev/blog/media/capture-conditions-2026-10-27/comparison.png)\n\n*Each tile represents one version capture. This selected overlap is not an estimate of error rates across MCP servers.*\n\nHistorical version attribution had an important limitation: HISTOR had not recorded the package version on each observation. The comparison used list contents and npm publication times to connect historical observations to release windows. That missing provenance needed a code fix of its own.\n\n## A launch argument can change the contract\n\nThe MongoDB differences affected versions 3.0.5 and 3.1.0. The bare launch exposed nine additional write tools. Other tools and descriptions differed too.\n\nThis matters when a client approves a tool list. An observation made with a read-only launch cannot establish which tools the same package advertises under another configuration. The launch entry belongs beside the captured definitions.\n\nIt also changes the question a comparison should answer. Before investigating a changed tool list, check whether the two captures used equivalent arguments and configuration. The [MongoDB capture notes](https://github.com/Paraphern/rugsnare/blob/a11024e7ad1f7f8a6e328c90ddb7457c18b22dcb/docs/servers/mongodb.md) preserve the peer's measurement context; our comparison records the bare-launch difference.\n\n## Startup network access can change registration\n\nFor `@netlify/mcp` 1.19.0, RugSnare captured `netlify-coding-rules`; HISTOR did not. Registration depends on fetching a topic list during startup. HISTOR's sandbox has no route to the internet.\n\nA tool absent under those conditions may still be present in a connected deployment. Capturing `tools/list` records what that instance advertised, under that launch. The [Netlify notes](https://github.com/Paraphern/rugsnare/blob/a11024e7ad1f7f8a6e328c90ddb7457c18b22dcb/docs/servers/netlify.md) make the capture window and corrections inspectable.\n\nNetwork policy therefore belongs in the observation record. So does authentication context: an anonymous or placeholder-key session cannot establish everything a real authenticated client receives.\n\n## The observer can retain tools the package stopped serving\n\nSix other version snapshots contained stale entries: two each for Shopify, Currents and Netlify. Paraphern checked the findings and confirmed that an automated re-pin had run over dirty capture environments. All six were re-captured from clean environments.\n\nThe [Shopify erratum](https://github.com/Paraphern/rugsnare/blob/a11024e7ad1f7f8a6e328c90ddb7457c18b22dcb/docs/servers/shopify.md) names the cross-check and records the corrected five-tool inventories for 1.16.0 and 1.17.0. The [Currents](https://github.com/Paraphern/rugsnare/blob/a11024e7ad1f7f8a6e328c90ddb7457c18b22dcb/docs/servers/currents.md) and Netlify pages preserve their corrections too.\n\nThis is why independently collected records are useful even when both collectors already publish hashes. A digest faithfully identifies the bytes its producer captured. The capture still needs to be the intended one.\n\nParaphern also incorporated a correction to our profile's description in the [comparison document](https://github.com/Paraphern/rugsnare/blob/a11024e7ad1f7f8a6e328c90ddb7457c18b22dcb/audits/drift-watch/comparison-dominion-captures.md). Our separate extras digest covers more than annotations. Writing down exactly which members a digest includes is part of making comparisons possible.\n\n## What we changed on our side\n\nFive overlapping packages had no tool list in HISTOR. Their launch requirements exposed gaps in our coverage: filesystem roots, an authentication mode, a start subcommand, a transport option, or a network dependency. A missing capture remained missing coverage.\n\nHISTOR's code now stores `packageVersion` and a launch record on each package observation. The timeline and `package_observations.jsonl.gz` expose the version, observer, image, runtime, entry and supplied configuration. Older rows remain `null` where the facts were never recorded.\n\nIn version 0.4.2, we also shipped four reviewed launch defaults:\n\n| Package | Supplied test configuration |\n|---|---|\n| Filesystem | The disposable container's `/work/app` directory |\n| Azure DevOps | A synthetic organization, envvar authentication and a placeholder token |\n| LaunchDarkly | The `start` command, stdio transport and a per-run placeholder |\n| Figma | `--stdio` and a placeholder environment variable |\n\nExplicit registry arguments take precedence. A previous failure can retry with the new configuration while retaining its earlier observation. The sandbox generates placeholder values locally; it receives no real credentials and gains no internet route.\n\nWe fixed another attribution error: when the observer omits its resolved version, the reader now leaves it unknown instead of substituting the version requested by the crawler.\n\n**These follow-up changes ship in [aimarket-histor 0.4.2](https://pypi.org/project/aimarket-histor/0.4.2/).** Both standalone sandbox observers were updated before the production HISTOR service on 27 October. The local HISTOR suite passed 610 tests, with 210 PostgreSQL cases skipped without a test database, one optional token-count case skipped without `tiktoken`, and 12 integration cases deselected. The new profile regressions use synthetic package responses and a stubbed container boundary. They do not establish four new successful captures of current upstream packages. Supabase and other services requiring a real authenticated network session can still remain unobserved.\n\n## A small comparison you can run yourself\n\nSave two complete `tools/list` arrays as `a.json` and `b.json`. This Python example reports differences in the three shared fields used above:\n\n```python\nimport json\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nFIELDS = (\"name\", \"description\", \"inputSchema\")\n\ndef surface(path):\n    tools = json.loads(Path(path).read_text())\n    if not isinstance(tools, list):\n        raise ValueError(\"Expected a complete tools/list array\")\n    result = {}\n    for tool in tools:\n        name = tool[\"name\"]\n        if name in result:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Duplicate tool name: {name}\")\n        result[name] = {\n            key: json.dumps(tool[key], sort_keys=True, allow_nan=False)\n            for key in FIELDS if key in tool\n        }\n    return result\n\na, b = map(surface, sys.argv[1:3])\nprint(\"Added:\", sorted(b.keys() - a.keys()))\nprint(\"Removed:\", sorted(a.keys() - b.keys()))\nfor name in sorted(a.keys() \u0026 b.keys()):\n    changed = [key for key in FIELDS if a[name].get(key) != b[name].get(key)]\n    if changed:\n        print(name, changed)\n```\n\nRun it with `python compare_captures.py a.json b.json`. It compares saved JSON values, preserving missing versus explicit `null` fields and distinguishing booleans from numbers. It does not implement MTL/1, classify compatibility, or verify capture provenance. Array order remains significant; `outputSchema` and extras are deliberately outside this example.\n\n![Four parts of capture context: exact package identity, launch configuration, runtime and dependencies, and network and authentication conditions.](https://modelmarket.dev/blog/media/capture-conditions-2026-10-27/capture-context.png)\n\n*A checklist for reproducible capture. HISTOR does not yet export resolved dependency inventories.*\n\nKeep both original responses and the conditions that produced them: package version, launch entry and arguments, configuration policy, image identity, resolved dependencies, network access and observation time. Establish the shared comparison fields before interpreting different digest strings.\n\nThe next useful cross-check is a comparison of fresh captures with equivalent launch conditions and explicit version records on both sides. That would test whether these changes make the join easier; this historical comparison cannot establish that result in advance.\n\n*Disclosure: we build HISTOR and WARDEN. AI assistance was used for the analysis, code, writing and cover illustration. The two diagrams are generated deterministically from the reported comparison and its documented limits. The cover is an editorial illustration, not a screenshot or measured result.*\n","user":{"name":"Alex","username":"alexar76","twitter_username":"build_ai_infra","github_username":null,"user_id":3927872,"website_url":"https://github.com/alexar76","profile_image":"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=640,height=640,fit=cover,gravity=auto,format=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Fuser%2Fprofile_image%2F3927872%2Fdf501cac-6862-47af-8b22-4e3067696337.jpeg","profile_image_90":"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=90,height=90,fit=cover,gravity=auto,format=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Fuser%2Fprofile_image%2F3927872%2Fdf501cac-6862-47af-8b22-4e3067696337.jpeg"}}